Subject: [PATCH] drbdstatus: tolerate a peer-less resource in `drbdsetup show --json`

The promoter's split-brain-avoidance detector (`get_split_brain_avoidance_policy`
-> `drbdstatus::get`) parses `drbdsetup show --show-defaults --json <res>` into
`drbdstatus::Resource`, whose `connections` field is required.

For a single-node / peer-less resource (zero connection stanzas, e.g. a
`connection-mesh { hosts self; }`), `drbdsetup show --json` omits the
`connections` key entirely -- unlike `drbdsetup status --json`, which emits an
empty `"connections": []`. serde therefore fails with

    missing field `connections` at line N column M

and the promoter logs `IGNORING resource '<res>'` for *every* events2 change/exists
event, so `process_drbd_event` never runs for that resource: its reactive
state (may_promote, start/stop reactions) goes stale. The resource is still
adopted once by the initial adjust pass, so it limps in steady state, but any
subsequent event-driven transition is silently dropped.

Mark `connections` `#[serde(default)]` so an absent key deserializes to an empty
vector -- which is exactly correct for a resource with no peers. No behavioural
change for multi-node resources (the key is present there).

Reproduced with drbd-utils 9.33.0 + drbd-reactor 1.11.0; the same struct is
present on master.
---
 src/drbdstatus.rs | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/drbdstatus.rs b/src/drbdstatus.rs
--- a/src/drbdstatus.rs
+++ b/src/drbdstatus.rs
@@ -8,6 +8,10 @@
 pub struct Resource {
     pub resource: String,
     pub options: Options,
+    // A peer-less (single-node) resource has no connection stanzas, so
+    // `drbdsetup show --json` omits `connections` entirely rather than
+    // emitting an empty array; tolerate that instead of failing to parse.
+    #[serde(default)]
     pub connections: Vec<Connection>,
 }

